mn38:16.2 starts: These four kinds of nutriment have craving as their source,
mn38:16.3 starts: And this craving has what as its source…?
mn38:16.4 starts: Craving has feeling as its source…And this feeling
mn38:16.5 starts: And this feeling has what as its source…?
mn38:16.6 starts: Feeling has contact as its source…And this contact
mn38:16.7 starts: And this contact has what as its source…?
mn38:16.8 starts: Contact has the sixfold base as its source…And this
mn38:16.9 starts: And this sixfold base has what as its source…?
mn38:16.10 starts: The sixfold base has mentality-materiality as its source…And this
mn38:16.11 starts: And this mentality-materiality has what as its source…?
mn38:16.12 starts: Mentality-materiality has consciousness as its source…And this
mn38:16.13 starts: And this consciousness has what as its source…?
mn38:16.14 starts: Consciousness has formations as its source…And these
mn38:16.15 starts: And these formations have what as their source,
mn38:16.16 starts: Formations have ignorance as their source, ignorance as their origin;
mn38:17.4 starts: with mentality-materiality as condition,
mn38:17.5 starts: the sixfold base; with the sixfold base as condition, contact;
mn38:18.3 starts: “Ageing and death have birth as condition, venerable sir.
mn38:18.4 starts: Thus we take it in this case: ‘With birth as condition, ageing and death.’”
mn38:18.6 starts: “‘With being as condition, birth’: so it was said.
mn38:18.7 starts: Now, bhikkhus, does birth have being as condition
mn38:18.9 starts: “Birth has being as condition, venerable sir.
mn38:18.11 starts: “‘With clinging as condition, being’: so it was said.
mn38:18.13 starts: “Being has clinging as condition,
mn38:18.45 starts: “‘With formations as condition, consciousness’: so it was said.
mn38:18.49 starts: ‘With formations as condition, consciousness.’”
mn38:18.50 starts: “‘With ignorance as condition, formations’: so it was said.
mn38:18.51 starts: Now, bhikkhus, do formations have ignorance as condition
mn38:18.53 starts: “Formations have ignorance as condition,
mn38:19.7 starts: with mentality-materiality as condition,
mn38:19.8 starts: the sixfold base; with the sixfold base as condition, contact;
mn38:21.20 starts: ‘With the cessation of craving,
mn38:21.25 starts: ‘With the cessation of feeling,
mn38:21.30 starts: ‘With the cessation of contact,
mn38:21.51 starts: ‘With the cessation of ignorance, cessation of formations’: so it was said.
mn38:21.52 starts: Now, bhikkhus, do formations cease with the cessation of ignorance
mn38:21.54 starts: “Formations cease with the cessation of ignorance, venerable sir.
mn38:22.1 starts: Recapitulation on Cessation “Good, bhikkhus.
mn38:29.5 starts: odours cognizable by the nose…
mn38:29.7 starts: tangibles cognizable by the body that are wished for,
mn38:30.1 starts: The Continuation of the Round “On seeing a form with the eye,
mn38:30.7 starts: “On hearing a sound with the ear…On smelling an odour with the nose…
mn38:30.8 none
mn38:30.11 starts: On cognizing a mind-object with the mind,
mn38:30.15 starts: Now delight in feelings is clinging. With his clinging as condition,
mn38:39.3 starts: With the stilling of applied and sustained thought,
mn38:41.1 starts: “On hearing a sound with the ear…On smelling an odour with the nose…
mn38:41.2 none
mn38:41.5 starts: On cognizing a mind-object with the mind,
mn38:41.7 none
mn38:41.9 starts: With the cessation of his delight comes cessation of clinging;
sn35.15:1.2 starts: Whatever gratification there is in the eye—
sn35.15:1.5 starts: Whatever danger there is in the eye—that I discovered.
sn35.15:1.6 starts: I have clearly seen with wisdom just how far the danger
sn35.15:1.8 starts: Whatever escape there is from the eye—that I discovered.
sn35.15:1.9 starts: I have clearly seen with wisdom just how far the escape
sn35.15:1.24 none
sn35.15:1.27 starts: Whatever escape there is from the mind—
sn35.15:2.2 starts: But when I directly knew all this as it really is,
